    "id": "p40-q74-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "74",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equation.\n$$6^x-9^x=9(2^x-3^x)$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=0,\\ 2$.\n\nFactorise to $(2^x-3^x)(3^x-9)=0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2^x3^x-(3^x)^2-9(2^x-3^x)&=0\\\\3^x(2^x-3^x)-9(2^x-3^x)&=0\\\\(2^x-3^x)(3^x-9)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $2^x=3^x$ or $3^x=9$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac23\\right)^x&=1\\\\x&=0,\\end{align*}$$\nor $3^x=3^2$, giving $x=2$.\n\nAt $x=0$, both sides are $0$. At $x=2$, both sides are $-45$. Hence $x=0,2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
